## What to deliver

Author the discharge system operation by operation — the searing discharge core, the
thin streaked forward bolt, and the flicker of crackle motes (as timed bursts at the
shot instant), with the forces and per-particle curves (including a velocity stretch
on the bolt) that make it lance forward and fade as the brief describes, and the
timeline kept **one-shot** — running `particle-3d render` to simulate and check the
effect as you go. When the simulated `effect.gif` reads as a single rail-lance energy
discharge that decays cleanly to empty, run `render` one last time and stop: the
recorded `actions.json` (and the `system.json` it emits) is your finished submission.
